annerist elongation and spatial tension"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-b909ab5af9f5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Elongated bodies, complex poses and ambiguous space can distinguish Mannerist experiments from ideals of balance. It is not merely bad anatomical drawing."},{"id":"LE102-01a2e0af909b2557","title":"Diet of Worms","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diet_of_Worms","aliases":["Diet of Worms"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01122","ARCHED-NEW101-0489"],"tapestryIds":["t63-fbe0eb4f286c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Luther before Charles V."},{"id":"LE102-5cc139e61b45ed75","title":"Erasmus portrait: Holbein version","kind":"art","reference":"https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/paintings/hans-holbein-the-younger-erasmus","aliases":["Erasmus portrait: Holbein version"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=22810b4b317a1e4b1f3e430f.webp","credit":"Hans Holbein the Younger","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holbein%2C_Hans_%28II%29_-_Erasmus_-_National_Gallery.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-9a1930a62417"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Holbein made several portraits of Erasmus; date and version need distinction.","creator":"Hans Holbein the Younger"},{"id":"LE102-c767cf8723e841cd","title":"Pierre de Ronsard","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre_de_Ronsard","aliases":["Pierre de Ronsard"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-7ac6b9e0f443"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"French Renaissance poet."},{"id":"LE102-64f0fd69e53b469c","title":"Battle of Pavia","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pavia","aliases":["Battle of Pavia"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-3cc224d8b219"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Francis I captured."},{"id":"L