:"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Separation%20of%20powers","aliases":["Separation of powers"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0114"],"tapestryIds":["t69-105d16ded3e3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Montesquieu's analysis distinguishes legislative, executive and judicial power. It should not be confused with Rousseau's account of the general will."},{"id":"LE102-4214603fac8b7711","title":"Jacques-Louis David","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacques-Louis_David","aliases":["Jacques-Louis David"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04359","ALPHA-B002-Q132","PDF33-Q061-B"],"tapestryIds":["t63-3c4125b963c3"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Painter."},{"id":"LE102-574113623e9cac36","title":"Tom Jones","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_History_of_Tom_Jones,_a_Foundling","aliases":["Tom Jones"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q01357"],"tapestryIds":["t63-b2e6b216b7c9"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Novel first published in 1749.","creator":"Henry Fielding"},{"id":"LE102-2166b82cb6161b8e","title":"Imaginary Prisons: first edition","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carceri_d'invenzione","aliases":["Imaginary Prisons: first edition"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0d7fa8af48b86525ad9b7095.webp","credit":"Giovanni Battista Piranesi","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Battista_Piranesi_-_Le_Carceri_d%27Invenzione_-_First_Edition_-_1750_-_01_-_Metropolitan_DP828185.jpg","caption":"Title plate from the first edition, c.1750; distinguish the more heavily reworked second edition of 1761."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0d7fa8af48b86525ad9b7095.webp","credit":"Giovanni Battista Piranesi","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Battista_Piranesi_-_Le_Carceri_d%27Invenzione_-_First_Edition_-_1750_-_01_-_Metropolitan_DP828185.jpg","licenseUrl":""}],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q03973","GEN43-Q03974"],"tapestryIds":["t63-6d281d184032"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Etching series; substantially reworked second edition in 1761.","creator":"Giovanni Battista Piranesi","assetIds":["T82-t63-6d281d184032"]},{"id":"LE102-305898b984a42b27","title":"Johann Wolfgang von Goethe","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Wolfgang_von_Goethe","aliases":["Johann Wolfgang von Goethe"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-51b4582f6c0c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Writer."},{"id":"LE102-a10fd6aef1afe80f","title":"Neoclassicism","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neoclassicism","aliases":["Neoclassicism"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-f682dc960939"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Approximate stylistic framework; classical revival has earlier precedents and later continuations."},{"id":"LE102-6b3e90cd41c6cf4e","title":"Neoclassicism and archaeological knowledge","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Neoclassicism%20and%20archaeological%20knowledge","aliases":["Neoclassicism and archaeological knowledge"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-7fd7f3577cc1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Interest in antiquity, archaeology and Winckelmann's writing informed a renewed classical vocabulary. Ancient subject matter alone does not distinguish Neoclassicism from Renaissance art."},{"id":"LE102-914279b1e12847db","title":"The Grand Tour and collecting antiquity","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Grand%20Tour%20and%20collecting%20antiquity","aliases":["The Grand Tour and collecting antiquity"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-cf747a928cc4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Elite educational travel supported markets in antiquities, copies, portraits and views. Distinguish a souvenir veduta from a neutral photographic record."},{"id":"LE102-0c1c8191d0aa7b0c","title":"Veduta and capriccio","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Veduta%20and%20capriccio","aliases":["Veduta and capriccio"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-fc22f462458d"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"A veduta presents a recognisable view; a capriccio combines or invents architectural motifs. Artists may alter a real view for pictorial purposes."},{"id":"LE102-7d97f28536c9b538","title":"Cast iron, wrought iron and steel","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Cast%20iron%2C%20wrought%20iron%20and%20steel","aliases":["Cast iron, wrought iron and steel"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-38822936c244"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"These iron-based materials differ in manufacture and structural behaviour. Their architectural use cannot be inferred from colour or a modern label alone.","built":"1750"},{"id":"LE102-37eacec145332275","title":"Industrialisation and urbanisation","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Industrialisation%20and%20urbanisation","aliases":["Industrialisation and urbanisation"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-ecf6c5cbe372"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Factory production, transport networks and migration altered cities and labour. Industrial change happened at different rates across countries and sectors."},{"id":"LE102-ea720c39e9ef527e","title":"Encyclopédie","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encyclop%C3%A9die","aliases":["Encyclopédie"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t63-6119c0e3ef30"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Original text and plate volumes; later supplements are separate.","creator":"Denis Diderot, Jean le Rond d'Alembert"},{"id":"LE102-640cb5b483e7bc32","title":"Richard Brinsley Sheridan","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Brinsley_Sheridan","aliases"