ions","aliases":["The Salon and independent exhibitions"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t69-52ca5b3944f4"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Juries, official exhibitions, dealers and independent shows shaped careers and public reception. Rejection from the Salon and participation in Impressionist exhibitions are different histories."},{"id":"LE102-17933ba24c211443","title":"Crystal Palace","kind":"architecture","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Crystal%20Palace","aliases":["Crystal Palace"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04324","ARCHED-B100-20261007-008","ARCHED-NEW101-0183","ARCHED-NEW101-0240","ARCHED-NEW101-0424","ALPHA-B001-Q068","ALPHA-B004-Q349","ALPHA-B010-Q906","PDF35-Q078-A","PDF35-CON-015-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-0d2522cb46bf"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Prefabricated iron and glass housed the Great Exhibition; the original Hyde Park structure was later relocated.","built":"1851","creator":"Joseph Paxton","city":"London","style":"Iron-and-glass architecture","era":"Nineteenth century","resolvedTitle102":"Crystal Palace"},{"id":"LE102-03b31a67d429dc09","title":"Foucault's public pendulum demonstration","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foucault_pendulum","aliases":["Foucault's public pendulum demonstration"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0497"],"tapestryIds":["t63-fa4bb4bc17e1"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Paris Panthéon; a marginal annotation in IMG_3636."},{"id":"LE102-43b57e804e0a7735","title":"Great Exhibition in London","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Great%20Exhibition%20in%20London","aliases":["Great Exhibition in London"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-08e73f3779d6"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Industrial production and global display were housed in Joseph Paxton's Crystal Palace."},{"id":"LE102-60f3365a5b3238b0","title":"Louis-Napoleon's coup d'état","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Louis-Napoleon%27s%20coup%20d%27%C3%A9tat","aliases":["Louis-Napoleon's coup d'état"],"photos":[],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-27f6e62af73c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The coup of 2 December ended the parliamentary basis of the Second Republic."},{"id":"LE102-e2fcadf499e8b539","title":"Ophelia","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Ophelia","aliases":["Ophelia"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=8e67ca2b55e97439fea57458.webp","credit":"John Everett Millais","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Everett_Millais_-_Ophelia_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."}],"questionIds":[],"tapestryIds":["t68-a59364ea2a28"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Pre-Raphaelite painting after Shakespeare's Hamlet, combining literary subject and detailed vegetation.","creator":"John Everett Millais"},{"id":"LE102-2ae3a34ddea7ef58","title":"French Second Empire proclaimed","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=French%20Second%20Empire%20proclaimed","aliases":["French Second Empire proclaimed"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0520"],"tapestryIds":["t68-924e52cbdc8c"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Louis-Napoleon became Napoleon III; distinguish him from Napoleon I."},{"id":"LE102-8fb993caed2b3afd","title":"Crimean War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Crimean%20War","aliases":["Crimean War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["GEN43-Q04150","ARCHED-NEW101-0526","ALPHA-B002-Q122","ALPHA-B002-Q148","ALPHA-B010-Q924"],"tapestryIds":["t68-c0268a877fe2"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Russia fought an alliance including the Ottoman Empire, Britain and France; Piedmont-Sardinia joined in 1855."},{"id":"LE102-2511457895ed4bdf","title":"Vincent van Gogh","kind":"person","ref