 displayed in his independent pavilion.","creator":"Gustave Courbet","assetIds":["PDFART48-145"]},{"id":"LE102-26123c74503e6bee","title":"Treaty of Paris ends Crimean War","kind":"history","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Treaty%20of%20Paris%20ends%20Crimean%20War","aliases":["Treaty of Paris ends Crimean War"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-NEW101-0526"],"tapestryIds":["t68-adf317fb83a0"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"The settlement restricted Russian naval power in the Black Sea and altered European diplomacy."},{"id":"LE102-c1b8f895b068171e","title":"Sigmund Freud","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Sigmund%20Freud","aliases":["Sigmund Freud"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ALPHA-B002-Q164","ALPHA-B003-Q250"],"tapestryIds":["t68-66c1b6c7e033"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Founder of psychoanalysis; lived and worked in Vienna before exile in London."},{"id":"LE102-5b3b6a7143318a89","title":"Madame Bovary","kind":"person","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Madame%20Bovary","aliases":["Madame Bovary"],"photos":[],"questionIds":["ARCHED-B03-20261007-450","PDF34-Q-016-A"],"tapestryIds":["t68-8f7b4dba05b5"],"museumIds":[],"mapIds":[],"note":"Realist prose examines provincial life and desire; distinguish literary Realism from identical dates in painting.","creator":"Gustave Flaubert"},{"id":"LE102-b806d8aac7c7cf0a","title":"The Gleaners","kind":"art","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Gleaners","aliases":["The Gleaners"],"photos":[{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0f6899a6a3a23bf6445a16f7.webp","credit":"Jean-François Millet","license":"Public domain","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean-Fran%C3%A7ois_Millet_-_Gleaners_-_Google_Art_Project_2.jpg","caption":"Identified work. Sculpture photographs may show later casts or surviving copies."},{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=0f6899a6a3a23bf6445a16f7.webp","cr